# 🤝 Team Collaboration Guide


## 🌿 Our Branches
- **`main`**: Production-ready code only. This is our "Golden Copy."
- **`uat`**: Testing branch. This is where we verify that Frontend and Backend work together.
- **`dev`**: Our daily workshop. All features meet here first.

---

## 🚀 Daily Workflow (The "Feature Branch" Method)

Follow these steps for every new task (e.g., "Add Status Bar"):

## The Rules:

- NEVER push directly to main or dev.

- ALWAYS create a new branch for every task (e.g., feat/add-login).

- Secrets: I’ve put the secrets in GitHub for the future, but for local work, you need to create a local .env file. (you can check them out on the repo and add them to the project locally)
make sure you do not push the .env file!

### 1. Sync & Start
Always start from the latest version of `dev`.
```bash
git checkout dev
git pull origin dev
git checkout -b feat/your-feature-name

### 2. Work & Commit
Code on your local machine. Save your progress with clear messages.
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "feat: added [description of work]"

### 3. Share & Review
Push your branch and open a Pull Request (PR) to merge into dev.
```bash
git push origin feat/your-feature-name

### Wait for your teammate to review and approve the PR before merging!

### 4. Security & Secrets

NEVER push the .env file to GitHub.

- Ensure .env is listed in your .gitignore.

- Use .env.example as a template for new keys.






